.TH HW-FAULT-EXPORTER 1 "2024-01-15" "arm-linux-fault-resilience" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hw-fault-exporter \- Prometheus exporter for ARM Linux hardware fault counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hw-fault-exporter
[\fB\-\-listen\-addr\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-sysfs\-root\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-metrics\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-scrape\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR]
[\fB\-\-once\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-edac\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-mce\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-aer\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hw-fault-exporter
scrapes hardware error counters from the Linux sysfs filesystem and exposes
them as Prometheus metrics. Three subsystems are covered:
.TP
.B EDAC
Error Detection And Correction \- DRAM correctable and uncorrectable error
counters from \fI/sys/devices/system/edac/\fR.
.TP
.B MCE
Machine Check Events \- processor hardware error events from ACPI APEI/GHES
or \fI/dev/mcelog\fR.
.TP
.B PCIe AER
Advanced Error Reporting \- PCIe correctable and uncorrectable error counters
from \fI/sys/bus/pci/devices/*/aer_dev_*\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-listen\-addr \fIADDR\fR
TCP address to listen on for Prometheus scrapes. Default: \fB:9101\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-sysfs\-root \fIPATH\fR
Root of the sysfs filesystem. Override for testing with a mock sysfs tree.
Default: \fB/sys\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-path \fIPATH\fR
HTTP path for the Prometheus metrics endpoint. Default: \fB/metrics\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level \fILEVEL\fR
Logging verbosity. One of: \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBerror\fR.
Default: \fBinfo\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-scrape\-timeout \fIDURATION\fR
Maximum time allowed for a single scrape cycle, e.g. \fB10s\fR, \fB30s\fR.
Default: \fB10s\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Single-shot mode: scrape all collectors once, print metrics in Prometheus
text format to stdout, and exit. No HTTP server is started. Useful with
cron and node_exporter's textfile collector.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-edac
Disable the EDAC collector.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mce
Disable the MCE collector.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aer
Disable the PCIe AER collector.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B /metrics
Prometheus text-format metrics. Scraped by Prometheus at the configured
interval.
.TP
.B /healthz
Liveness probe. Returns HTTP 200 while the process is running.
.TP
.B /readyz
Readiness probe. Returns HTTP 503 until the first successful \fI/metrics\fR
scrape completes, then returns 200. Used by Kubernetes to delay traffic
until the exporter is warmed up.
.SH METRICS
.TP
.B edac_correctable_errors_total{controller, csrow, channel}
Cumulative correctable EDAC errors per channel since boot.
.TP
.B edac_uncorrectable_errors_total{controller, csrow}
Cumulative uncorrectable EDAC errors per csrow since boot.
.TP
.B edac_controller_ce_total{controller}
Total correctable errors on the memory controller since boot.
.TP
.B edac_controller_ue_total{controller}
Total uncorrectable errors on the memory controller since boot.
.TP
.B pcie_aer_correctable_total{device, error_type}
Cumulative PCIe AER correctable errors per device.
.TP
.B pcie_aer_uncorrectable_total{device, error_type, severity}
Cumulative PCIe AER uncorrectable errors (nonfatal or fatal).
.TP
.B mce_events_total{severity, bank, source}
Total machine check events by severity and bank.
.TP
.B fault_resilience_collector_up{collector}
1 if the collector's sysfs path is accessible, 0 if the subsystem is absent.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the exporter on all interfaces, port 9101:
.PP
.nf
.RS
hw-fault-exporter \-\-listen\-addr :9101
.RE
.fi
.PP
Single-shot scrape for cron + textfile collector:
.PP
.nf
.RS
hw-fault-exporter \-\-once > /var/lib/node_exporter/fault.prom
.RE
.fi
.PP
Test against a mock sysfs tree:
.PP
.nf
.RS
hw-fault-exporter \-\-sysfs\-root /tmp/mock\-sysfs \-\-once
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or clean shutdown via SIGTERM/SIGINT).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (port in use, permission denied, etc.).
